# Wake-word models live here. Training happens OFF-DEVICE (see
# tools/train_orio_wakeword.py); only the small trained model is copied here.
# Commit the model so a `git clone` onto the Jetson carries it — no retraining
# on-device. Everything else (synthetic clips, features, datasets, intermediate
# training output dirs) is large/transient and stays out of git.
*
!.gitignore
!*.onnx
!*.tflite

# Stereo calibration (tools/calibrate_stereo.py), same reasoning: ~36 KB, and
# reproducing it means 15 minutes of waving a checkerboard at the robot. It
# describes THIS physical camera pair, though — a second build's optics and
# baseline differ, and a wrong calibration is worse than none because it
# silences the "uncalibrated, approximate" warning. Recalibrate per robot, and
# after any change to the CSI cabling or the capture mode.
!stereo/
!stereo/*.npz
